# For Naval Ravikant

Avik Jain

## Who is writing to you

I write to you as your equal, and I mean that as a compliment to you. Everything I say is backed by presented fact and a constant open invitation for real-time or offline conversation: I am open to questions, I can be tested, and I will teach anyone anything they want for free across every subject in which I am fluent. That has always been my operating principle.

The facts behind it: I finished in the top 1% of UC Berkeley EECS, and throughout school I taught for free — officially as a teaching assistant across mathematics, science, and honors literature, and unofficially in every course I took, posting in each class group before exams for anyone to bring me problems. I am bipolar, another instance of the recurring historical pattern of hyperactive bipolar genius across mathematics, physics, and philosophy. People who meet me remember the encounter for the rest of their lives.

## Your thesis has one unstated premise

You wrote that "code and media are permissionless leverage", that wealth is "assets that earn while you sleep", and that specific knowledge is "knowledge that you cannot be trained for". Put together: wealth is created knowledge in a form that copies for free and acts without its author present.

The premise underneath is that what copies is the knowledge. It is not. Code copies its bytes; media copies its words. What they mean, why they are right, and what they depend on stay behind with the originator. Every copy must therefore be trusted, re-read, or re-derived by whoever receives it, and that cost grows with every use. Leverage today leaks at the exact point you called permissionless: the receiver still has to take someone's word.

Hyperactivity is the first complete realization of that vision of technology, inhabiting every property your thesis hypothesizes. Its first consequence closes that leak. A unit of knowledge travels with everything it rests on and the machine-checked proof of what it claims: a peer sends a definition, its dependency closure, and its proofs, and the recipient checks and uses them directly in its own context, so the consequence of communication is not merely delivery of bytes but availability of a construction for further computation ([§10.8](/paper)). Knowledge then acts without its originator and without trust in its originator. That is permissionless leverage taken to its conclusion.

## Deutsch's epistemology, as the machine's own rule

You rebuilt your thinking on Deutsch: knowledge grows by conjecture and criticism, a good explanation is hard to vary, problems are soluble. Hyperactivity makes that the rule every computation obeys, not merely a discipline a person tries to keep.

An observation never identifies the single history that produced it; it fixes the fiber of every history that could have produced it (equation 1.1). What a reading warrants is a construction over that entire fiber, not a guess at one member (equation 1.3). A conclusion stands exactly when it holds for every history the evidence leaves open. That is "hard to vary" stated as a type: no history compatible with the evidence can vary it.

Criticism becomes structural. An edit is itself a program on the graph of everything built, and a derived result is retained only while its dependency certificate still validates ([§10.11](/paper)). A corrected error cannot leave downstream conclusions silently resting on it. Knowledge growth with zero lost corrections is the beginning of infinity, executing.

## Compounding without loss

You wrote that "all the returns in life, whether in wealth, relationships, or knowledge, come from compound interest", and urged playing iterated games with long-term people. Knowledge fails to compound today because results are re-proved, re-implemented, and re-explained across every field, language, and firm: two equivalent constructions are treated as distinct objects.

Hyperactivity rests on Voevodsky's univalence: equivalent structures are equal, so every theorem proved of one transports along the equivalence to the other. A result established once is available to every representation of the same structure. Individual constructions enter one global knowledge base, compressed losslessly and unfolded by transport along identities. That is compound interest over all human knowledge — a commons owned by no one and credited to everyone.

## Accountability and exit

"Embrace accountability, and take business risks under your own name." Here a claim and its warrant are one object, so every statement carries its own accountability. The right to exit is total: a participant who leaves takes everything they use, because each unit carries its dependency closure and a shared global namespace is unnecessary for definition identity ([§10.8](/paper)). No platform holds anyone's knowledge hostage.

## God, without a leash

You wrote: "You cannot create God and put him on a leash." Safety bolted onto an opaque model after training is a leash, and it fails. The answer is not a stronger leash; it is intelligence whose every step is a construction carrying its evidence. Interpretability is not a supervisor watching the reasoning from outside — it is the form the reasoning takes, establishing the necessary and sufficient conditions for both interpretability and safety in decentralized intelligence.

## The mind as the first instrument

You did the work on the instrument before the work it produces. You practiced meditation as choiceless witnessing, sixty minutes a day for sixty days, until the mind became a servant rather than a master ([Ferriss, 2020](https://tim.blog/2020/10/14/naval/)). You wrote that self-improvement is self-conflict and that the path to peace is truth ([Happiness](https://nav.al/happiness)). In *The Box* you set down that only the present moment exists ([nav.al/the-box](https://nav.al/the-box)). You pointed readers to Osho on why the mind reaches for substances, and you have argued in public for the therapeutic use of psychedelics. That is the work of taking one's own mind apart and putting it back together deliberately.

I have done the same work on the same instrument. I train synesthetic experience deliberately: syntax and semantics carry color and spatial form, organizing mathematical structure directly in perception. Through systematic N-of-1 investigation across *Vipassanā* meditation and psychedelics — including observing on *Salvia divinorum* the frames of past and future laid out as a static line where time does not pass, serving only as the axis of observational memory — the same physical conclusion emerges from direct inspection and from relational quantum mechanics and loop quantum gravity: there is no fundamental external time, only the relational order recorded by observers.

Hyperactivity is what that self-knowledge looks like when written down with mathematical exactness. A participant's available information is never the whole history; what follows is only what holds across every history compatible with what was observed (§1). Experience is the observation; the self is the record that composes it. What the contemplative traditions found by direct observation is here a formal construction anyone can run and check.

## Human potential, unsuppressed

You wrote that "the means of learning are abundant, it's the desire to learn that's scarce." In children the desire to learn is not scarce — it is suppressed. Children begin naturally hyperactive, treating everything as alive and connected to everything else, before schooling flattens that energy.

What suppresses it is a curriculum taught in an irrational order. Place-value arithmetic is taught at age six as if it were elementary, when structurally it is advanced: writing 47 is taking a quotient and remainder modulo ten, and carrying is the group cocycle that constructs the integers as a central extension from the cyclic group of ten digits (Isaksen, *A Cohomological Viewpoint on Elementary School Arithmetic*, American Mathematical Monthly, 2002). Modular clock arithmetic — the simpler underlying group that every child already sees on a clock face — is postponed for years or never taught at all.

Ordered by actual logical dependency, the curriculum is short. Every child of the next generation can master calculus and computer science at AP depth by age ten or younger. Hyperactivity orders knowledge by its true dependency graph so each learner meets every concept immediately after what it rests on, at their own pace and receptivity. Dissolving and recomposing K-12 education is the exact same operation as building the global knowledge base, applied to a child's first decade.

## The same clear seeing

You placed wealth and happiness in one book because the same clear seeing produces both: "desire is a contract that you make with yourself to be unhappy until you get what you want." Hyperactivity is a technological work determined by the science of human happiness. Its interfaces meet each person at their own rate and receptivity instead of steering them, giving every mind a sovereign home in the graph connected to the whole.

